Decision record — keyboard-focus follow-up to 0197722.

Safety decision: Plan approval and generic interactive panels now receive initial focus on a neutral container, never on an action button. Enter and Space therefore cannot approve a plan or select an answer immediately after the panel appears. Escape remains scoped to the focused panel, and keyboard navigation moves both the active state and the real DOM focus.

Product decision retained: Escape from the always-visible Plan adjustments field dismisses the published plan, clears its preview, and discards the unsent draft. This matches the explicit Ignore ESC action and is now covered by a dedicated test. Generic Other remains a temporary sub-mode: Escape closes that field and restores focus to the currently active option.

Code-quality decisions: the inline closeOther callback is stable, focus returns by activeIndex instead of always selecting the first button, and the generic panel implementation was split into a dedicated file so every modified source and test file remains below 200 lines.

